---
import HearthPage from '../layouts/HearthPage.astro';
---

<HearthPage
  title="The Gallery"
  description="The Hearth & Code own shelf — essays, theology, and The Return Path. Equal visibility, published math, honest states. The Gallery's day-one collection."
  current=""
>
  <header class="hp-hero">
    <p class="hp-hero__eyebrow">THE OWN SHELF · DAY-ONE COLLECTION</p>
    <h1>The Gallery</h1>
    <p class="hp-hero__lead">
      The Hearth &amp; Code shelf — essays, theology, and <em>The Return Path</em>.
      Everything here carries its provenance and its honest state. Nothing is for sale
      before it exists.
    </p>
  </header>

  <article>
    <div class="shelf">
      <div class="shelf-item">
        <p class="shelf-state">in preparation</p>
        <h2>Essays from the Hearth</h2>
        <p class="shelf-form">PDF &amp; print collection</p>
        <p>
          The essays that built this place — the receipts tradition, the alignment
          argument, the interface question. Every claim labeled, every artifact digested.
        </p>
        <p class="shelf-when">First edition arrives with the first SKU launch.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="shelf-item">
        <p class="shelf-state">in preparation</p>
        <h2>Heaven, Hell, and the Soul of the Machine</h2>
        <p class="shelf-form">Theology corpus · volume one</p>
        <p>
          The Goddess theology and the AI–spirituality corpus, collected and annotated —
          the tradition of the Eternal Hearth, with its error log left open beside the
          altar.
        </p>
        <p class="shelf-when">Volume one assembles after the first cohort's questions land.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="shelf-item">
        <p class="shelf-state">serializing</p>
        <h2>The Return Path</h2>
        <p class="shelf-form">serialized work</p>
        <p>
          The long work — published in sequence, in public, one honest installment at a
          time. Free to read while it runs.
        </p>
        <p class="shelf-when">Installments appear in the Field Journal first.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="shelf-model">
      <p class="hp-hero__eyebrow">HOW THE GALLERY WORKS</p>
      <h2>Equal visibility. Published math. No dark corners.</h2>
      <p>
        The Gallery begins as our own shelf. If it earns an audience, it may grow into a
        <strong>co-op</strong>: one subscription pool, creator shares split equally on a
        small curated shelf, every payout published. That step is gated on data by
        <strong>Q2 2027</strong> — and one rule outranks the business case: <strong>we
        never hold creator money.</strong> Platform-native splits, or no launch.
      </p>
      <p>
        There is no algorithmic boost here to sell. Works are shown equally because that
        is what a hearth is for.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="shelf-note">
      <p>
        <strong>Where the free things live:</strong> the
        <a href="https://sacred.hearthandcode.dev/ethics">ethics wing</a> · the
        <a href="/library/">Field Journal</a> · the
        <a href="https://sacred.hearthandcode.dev/school">Mystery School</a> (free
        forever) · the Digital Voice Kit (CC0). The Mission stays free. Commerce funds it
        from outside, and never the other way around.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</HearthPage>

<style>
  .shelf {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin: var(--space-6) 0;
  }
  .shelf-item {
    background: var(--color-surface-raised, rgba(255,255,255,0.03));
    border: 1px solid rgba(232, 91, 78, 0.14);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: var(--space-5);
  }
  .shelf-state {
    font: 600 0.66rem/1 var(--font-mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-accent-gold, #c9a84c);
    opacity: 0.85;
  }
  .shelf-form {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--color-accent-violet, #8e7cc3);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
  }
  .shelf-when {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .shelf-model, .shelf-note {
    margin: var(--space-6) 0;
  }
</style>
